body:
`CollapsibleTrigger` is rendered `asChild` with a `<div>` that looks clickable, but a `div` is not keyboard-accessible by default and won’t expose correct button semantics to assistive tech. Use a semantic `<button>` (or add appropriate `role="button"`, `tabIndex=0`, and key handlers) so the section group can be toggled via keyboard.
```suggestion
      <CollapsibleTrigger className="flex items-center gap-2 pb-2 border-b cursor-pointer hover:bg-muted/50 transition-colors rounded-t-md px-2 py-1.5">
        {isCollapsed ? (
          <ChevronRight className="h-4 w-4 text-muted-foreground shrink-0" />
        ) : (
          <ChevronDown className="h-4 w-4 text-muted-foreground shrink-0" />
        )}
        {group.icon && <span className="text-muted-foreground">{group.icon}</span>}
        <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold">{group.title}</h3>
```
